{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1372525-charms-for-qcs","id":1372525,"title":"Charms for QCs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-03T13:29:53-08:00","id":1372525,"title":"Charms for QCs","content":"Does anyone have some helpful advice about building-- and perhaps more importantly, <i>balancing</i>-- Charms for NPCs? I've been having trouble finding the line between &quot;this is threatening&quot; and &quot;this is unfair bull****.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T13:47:59-08:00","id":1372530,"title":"","content":"A few guidelines I like to keep in mind:<br /> <br /> Willpower and health levels are the most limited resources most characters have - if you think a charm is powerful enough to only be used once or twice per combat or scene, give them wp or hl costs. <br /> <br /> In combat, motes come back at 5m per turn. Therefore, if a charm has a cost of 5m or less, it can be used every turn and not really drain the NPC's resources. In my experience, you rarely want to be using multiple charms for an NPC per turn in combat anyway, so its best to assume that most charms will be used on their own. I find it's simplest to give charm costs in multiples of 5m as well, since that keeps the math simpler on regeneration, and makes it easy to calculate &quot;how many rounds of combat will this take to regenerate?&quot;<br /> <br /> Conversely, essence doesn't regenerate during non-combat scenes, so higher mote costs there will be more restrictive. If a powerful spirit has a mote pool of 100 essence, and one of their social charms has a mote cost of 10m, they're basically not going to use that more than 10 times in the scene, and probably less, since they'll have other stuff they want to use too. As a consequence of this, charms that are required to defend against something that players can effectively &quot;spam&quot; (Read Intentions actions, for example, which by the letter of the rules, everyone can call for at any time) are reasonably priced when they defend against a whole bunch of people at once, or are quite cheap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T13:56:15-08:00","id":1372538,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately given the huge swing in power that can exist in between 2 characters, there are as many answers as there are PC circles.<br /> <br /> My rule of thumb is up accuracy but lower damage/effect. A QC who misses for the whole fight is just boring, but one who can reliably use super strong moves is not fun either.<br /> <br /> Also it's not actually important that the players actually be in real danger, so long as you can make them believe that they are. Focus on dramatic effects like creating hazards or putting a player in a dangerous but ultimately fixable position. Players will be too busy panicking to notice that the QC isn't actually strong enough to kill them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T14:34:04-08:00","id":1372545,"title":"","content":"I tend to just give my NPC &quot;whatever they need&quot; without necesarily writing anything specific down. A dusk caste abyssal murdermachine that the players have to defeat will of course have access to most of the abyssal combat charms, some resistance charms and then some - but it'll have a weakness. The weakness wont be easy to spot or notice, but it'll be there. Charms work just the same.<br /> <br /> As for making them threatening but not unfair - then that's... tricky. It all depends on how many combat capable characters you have between your players, how much resistance your players have to face before they give up (or how creative they are at solving their problems)<br /> <br /> Relatively weak player characters that exploit the few charms they have extremely well can easily take down even the cheesiest NPC - exalted is like that.<br /> <br /> <br /> that's why I don't use any hard rules for scaling NPC difficulty - I just give them 'enough'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T19:04:28-08:00","id":1372603,"title":"","content":"For whatever it's worth, my group is pretty well set up for combat-- everyone's got 4 or 5 dots in their combat attributes and abilities, and everyone's got at least a few fighting Charms. On the plus side, everyone's in the same general level of power. On the downside, that level is pretty damn high.<ul><li>The Dawn has mostly only invested in White Reaper. He's also got a Grand Grimcleaver that eats souls and spits out battle groups.</li> <li>The Night is a Dodge supernal; he also has a bit of Snake Style and a little more Throwing.</li> <li>The Eclipse has gone for Silver-Voiced Nightengale Style, along with a few of the Presence and Performance Charms that help out your allies.</li> <li>The Zenith has focused hard on Melee's defend other Charms. He's also well into the process of equipping everyone with artifacts.</li> <li>The Twilight has some defensive spells and a nifty artifact weapon that lets her make medium-ranged attacks with Perception + Occult and use sorcerous motes to enhance attacks. She's also working with the Zenith to awaken Evocations for everyone's artifacts.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T00:56:32-08:00","id":1372635,"title":"","content":"Mostly? I rarely bother. I don't want to track motes and Willpower. This mook has a 16 Accuracy attack and 8 Parry. Probably because it's using Charms or something. Don't worry about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}